Backend-only FastAPI service using uv, SQLite and systemd.
{% if enable_jobs %}
Includes Redis-backed ARQ workers and a separate interval scheduler.
{% endif %}

## Development

```bash
uv sync
cp .env.example .env
uv run {{ cli_command }} init-db
uv run {{ cli_command }} serve
```

Run commands from the project root. Python is selected from `.python-version`.
All commands and systemd services load the same `.env` automatically. Exported
environment variables override the file. Settings are loaded once per process;
restart services after changing configuration.

{% if enable_jobs %}
Install Redis (Ubuntu: `sudo apt install redis-server`) and start it before running the API.
In separate terminals:

```bash
uv run {{ cli_command }} worker
uv run {{ cli_command }} scheduler
uv run {{ cli_command }} enqueue "hello"
```

The scheduler sleeps for the configured interval between dispatches. Submissions
do not overlap. Missed executions during downtime are not replayed. ARQ is in
maintenance-only mode; the optional job feature remains supported by this template.
{% endif %}

## API

- `GET /health/live`: process liveness.
- `GET /health` or `GET /health/ready`: SQLite{% if enable_jobs %} and Redis{% endif %} readiness, returning 503 on dependency failure.
- `GET /messages/count`: sample persisted message count.
{% if enable_jobs %}
- `POST /jobs`: submit `{"message":"hello"}`, returning a job ID and HTTP 202.
{% endif %}
- `GET /docs`: interactive OpenAPI documentation.

Keep the default loopback binding unless authentication and network exposure
are explicitly configured.

## Ubuntu deployment

After running `uv sync` and configuring `.env`, execute:

```bash
sudo bash deploy/install.sh
sudo systemctl status {{ project_slug }}-api.service
sudo journalctl -fu {{ project_slug }}-api.service
```

The installer enables the API{% if enable_jobs %}, worker and scheduler{% endif %} at boot under a non-root account.
To update, run `uv sync --frozen --no-dev` as the service user and restart the installed units.
Commit the generated `uv.lock` to your repository.

## Tests

